// 9. Open questions
children.push(H("9. Open questions", HeadingLevel.HEADING_1));
children.push(P("The following questions are either explicitly posed in the recent literature or follow directly from the gaps it leaves. They are grouped from fundamental to campaign-specific."));
children.push(Num("Regime dependence of the LWP adjustment. Goren et al. (2026) and Zhou and Feingold (2023, as cited therein) find S_LWP varies by an order of magnitude with cloud morphology even among non-precipitating clouds. What sets the adjustment in a given boundary-layer state, and can it be predicted from measurable quantities such as cloud-base height, inversion strength, free-tropospheric humidity and cell size (Wood, 2007; Ackerman et al., 2004)?"));
children.push(Num("Causality versus co-variability. Zhang et al. (2025) argue for a causal entrainment-drying signal at EPCAPE; Goren et al. (2025) argue that inverted-V relationships are co-variability. Both call for LES under controlled meteorology. Which observational designs (Lagrangian tracking, regime stratification, counterfactual estimation) are sufficient to separate the two?"));
children.push(Num("Timescale of adjustments. Glassmeier et al. (2021) show ship tracks do not reach steady state; Wood (2007) finds the sign of the thickness response changes with time. How long do real stratocumulus fields take to adjust, and does that timescale exceed the residence time of a polluted air mass over a given site?"));
children.push(Num("Selection bias in natural experiments. Manshausen et al. (2022) find opposite LWP responses in visible and invisible tracks. What fraction of polluted clouds are represented by the visible subset, and how should opportunistic experiments be weighted when scaling to the globe (Christensen et al., 2022)?"));
children.push(Num("The competition response in polluted coastal air. Dedrick et al. (2026) find scavenging signatures overwhelm the competition signature at EPCAPE. Does the diminished Twomey effect at high aerosol seen at LASIC (Dedrick et al., 2025) also hold at a coastal site, and how does it depend on the aerosol size distribution class?"));
children.push(Num("Boundary-layer coupling. Decoupling removes about 60% of accumulation-mode particles from the cloud layer at ENA (Wang et al., 2026, preprint). How should surface aerosol be scaled to cloud base under partially coupled conditions, and does the EPCAPE radiosonde and lidar record allow a continuous coupling index rather than a binary flag?"));
children.push(Num("Retrieval circularity. If r_e is computed from LWC with an assumed N_d, it cannot respond to aerosol by construction (Huang et al., 2012). Which ARM products at EPCAPE are independent enough of each other, and of the aerosol measurements, to support a susceptibility analysis?"));
children.push(Num("Surface radiation. No study found tests whether surface shortwave transmission under marine stratocumulus varies with aerosol in the way the susceptibility formulas predict, and the one continental long-term study found no daily signal (Sena et al., 2016). Can a one-year coastal record, filtered to overcast, coupled, single-layer liquid clouds and binned by LWP, detect the expected signal, and what does 1-D closure with libRadtran (Emde et al., 2016) say the expected signal is?"));
children.push(Num("Spectral transition-zone information. The linear-mixing behavior of zenith radiance across cloud edges (Marshak et al., 2009) and the cloud-processed aerosol signature after dissipation (Eck et al., 2012) have not been exploited at a coastal stratocumulus site with hyperspectral surface instruments. Do pre-, in- and post-cloud spectra carry a usable aerosol signal?"));
children.push(Num("Pre-industrial baseline. Nearly half the ERFaci uncertainty traces to natural aerosol (Carslaw et al., 2013). Do the clean-marine periods at EPCAPE and other coastal sites provide usable analogs?"));

// 10. Reading roadmap
children.push(H("10. Suggested reading order", HeadingLevel.HEADING_1));
children.push(P("The list below is ordered for a reader with a radiation background who wants to reach the current debate efficiently. Papers already in the project folder are marked."));
children.push(Num("Twomey (1977) — the four-page original. Then Oreopoulos and Platnick (2006) for the susceptibility algebra.", "roadmap"));
children.push(Num("Albrecht (1989) and Pincus and Baker (1994) — the adjustment hypothesis in its optimistic form.", "roadmap"));
children.push(Num("Hoppel et al. (1986, 1996) — the Hoppel minimum, which the EPCAPE group uses heavily.", "roadmap"));
children.push(Num("Feingold et al. (2003) and McComiskey et al. (2009) — how ground-based ACI metrics are defined and why they spread. McComiskey et al. is the Point Reyes analog of EPCAPE.", "roadmap"));
children.push(Num("Ackerman et al. (2004, in folder), Bretherton et al. (2007), Wood (2007) — the entrainment–sedimentation feedback and the mixed-layer view.", "roadmap"));
children.push(Num("Stevens and Feingold (2009) — the buffered-system framing.", "roadmap"));
children.push(Num("Zhao et al. (2012), Huang et al. (2012), Lim et al. (2016) — read before using MICROBASE or NDROP.", "roadmap"));
children.push(Num("Sena et al. (2016) — the only long-term surface-radiation ACI study; a model for a defensible null result.", "roadmap"));
children.push(Num("Grosvenor et al. (2018) and Quaas et al. (2020) — the retrieval and constraint problems from the satellite side.", "roadmap"));
children.push(Num("Toll et al. (2019), Gryspeerdt et al. (2019), Glassmeier et al. (2021), Manshausen et al. (2022), Christensen et al. (2022) — the LWP adjustment debate.", "roadmap"));
children.push(Num("Bellouin et al. (2020) — the assessment that frames the forcing numbers.", "roadmap"));
children.push(Num("Feingold et al. (2022) and Goren et al. (2026) — the current susceptibility decomposition and the morphology-weighted result.", "roadmap"));
children.push(Num("Dedrick et al. (2025, 2026, in folder), Zhang et al. (2025), Chellappan et al. (2026) — the EPCAPE papers.", "roadmap"));
children.push(Num("Dong et al. (1997, 1998, in folder), Marshak et al. (2009), McBride et al. (2011), Gristey et al. (2020) — the surface-radiation toolkit.", "roadmap"));

